# Local Claude Code state stays ignored. The one exception is the shared,
# checked-in permission ruleset: .claude/settings.json (deny-only). Exclude the
# directory CONTENTS, not the directory itself — git cannot re-include a file
# inside an excluded directory.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/rules/
outputs/

# Playwright transient output (traces, screenshots on failure)
test-results/
playwright-report/

# Vite build output (PR-22): src/app/ is the committed source; public/ is
# regenerated by `npm run build` (see package.json prestart, and
# docs/ARCHITECTURE.md "Frontend build"). Never commit it.
/public/

# Live-retest harness screenshots (uploaded as CI artifacts, never committed)
live-retest-artifacts/

# Stage-A acceptance evidence — raw runs from the Phase 4 Stage-A streak (2026-08-01).
# The machinery that produced these was removed under its recorded sunset once Stage A
# reached 5/5, so nothing regenerates them — but the runs themselves are preserved locally
# and must NEVER be committed. Screenshots and full logs stay out of the repository; what
# enters it is the bounded, privacy-safe record per session under docs/verification/,
# carrying SHA-256 hashes of these files rather than the files.
canary-artifacts/
stage-a-artifacts/
rehearsal-artifacts/

# Supabase CLI transient/local state. Ignored because it is CLI working state
# that may carry local connection and configuration artifacts, including
# CREDENTIAL-BEARING data — connection strings and passwords the CLI writes or
# caches while linked. None of that belongs in version control, and the
# protection has to be structural rather than a remembered instruction, because
# the owner links inside this checkout to run `supabase db push`.
#
# NOT a project-reference rule. The owner ruled on 2026-08-09 that a Supabase
# PROJECT REFERENCE is non-secret project metadata — not a password, key, token,
# or authorization mechanism (§8.4 of docs/SUPABASE_HOT_PATH_MIGRATION.md). These
# paths are ignored for the credentials and machine-local state they can hold,
# not for the identifier.
#
# supabase/config.toml is deliberately NOT ignored. `supabase init` writes
# `project_id = "<local directory name>"` there, not the remote reference —
# verified by running the CLI (2.113.0) rather than assumed — so ignoring it
# would keep reviewable project configuration out of version control for no
# credential reason. Supabase's own guide says to commit the supabase directory.
#
# scan:secrets is a genuine second line of defence for the thing that matters:
# a credential-bearing Postgres URI is refused wherever it appears, under any
# variable name. It carries no identifier rule and needs none.
supabase/.temp/
supabase/.branches/
